# WebVAST frontend configuration (build-time, Vite).
#
# VITE_DEMO — set to "1" to force self-contained DEMO mode: the dashboard serves
# a captured sample scan entirely in the browser and makes no network requests.
# This is the right setting for a public/hosted build (e.g. Vercel), so no live
# scanner is ever exposed. If VITE_DEMO is unset, the app probes the backend at
# load and automatically falls back to demo mode when none is reachable.
#
#   VITE_DEMO=1
#
# VITE_API_BASE — base URL of the WebVAST backend API that YOU run.
#
#   Local development (default): leave UNSET. The Vite dev server proxies
#   relative "/api" requests to http://127.0.0.1:8000, so no value is needed.
#
#   Hosted frontend (e.g. Vercel) talking to a backend on your own machine:
#     VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:8000
#   Browsers treat http://localhost as a secure context, so an HTTPS Vercel
#   page is allowed to call it — but only from YOUR machine, where that
#   backend is reachable. The public URL is inert for anyone else.
#
#   Hosted frontend talking to a backend you host somewhere reachable:
#     VITE_API_BASE=https://your-backend.example
#   Must be HTTPS (an HTTPS page cannot call a plain-HTTP remote host), and
#   that backend must allow this frontend's origin via WEBVAST_CORS_ORIGINS.
#
# VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:8000
